_infant_Dionysus_by_Praxiteles.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":["PDF33-Q004-A"],"tapestryIds":["t63-31adce33da77"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Traditionally attributed to Praxiteles; attribution and date are disputed.","creator":"Praxiteles"},{"id":"LE102-d70dc839f2e06d8d","title":"Battle of Chaeronea","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Chaeronea_(338_BC)","aliases":["Battle of Chaeronea"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0537"],"tapestryIds":["t63-9543d1eff267"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Philip II defeats the Greek coalition."},{"id":"LE102-3d3fdcfc8c25ebed","title":"Campaigns of Alexander the Great","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_Alexander_the_Great","aliases":["Campaigns of Alexander the Great"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-7f46e9bcb349"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Campaign into the Persian Empire and beyond."},{"id":"LE102-1650e70032f102e8","title":"Apoxyomenos","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apoxyomenos","aliases":["Apoxyomenos"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0e3cf17e11cad777ad3db2bf.webp","credit":"Copy after Lysippos","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apoxyomenos_Pio-Clementino_Inv1185.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-7f2477080dca"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Lost Greek original; athlete scraping his body with a strigil.","creator":"Lysippos"},{"id":"LE102-be9d8f13af01656a","title":"Hellenistic drama and spatial movement","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Hellenistic%20drama%20and%20spatial%20movement","aliases":["Hellenistic drama and spatial movement"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-64e32ce7cfa6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Expanded poses, emotional intensity and engagement with surrounding space are useful comparisons with Classical balance, though both periods contain varied works."},{"id":"LE102-05a48162fadcf122","title":"Roman arch, vault and dome","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Roman%20arch%2C%20vault%20and%20dome","aliases":["Roman arch, vault and dome"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-ba02f6038e86"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"An arch spans an opening; a barrel vault extends the arch; intersecting barrel vaults form a groin vault. A dome covers a central space. Do not treat all four as synonyms.","built":"-300"},{"id":"LE102-c5e897ef76649ec4","title":"First Punic War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Punic_War","aliases":["First Punic War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-880cd69eaee7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Rome and Carthage."},{"id":"LE102-fef325fa2cf920db","title":"Parthian Empire","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parthian_Empire","aliases":["Parthian Empire"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-e28cb1002606"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Arsacid kingdom; the founding date is also given as 247 BCE."},{"id":"LE102-9e750052ec2702bc","title":"Second Punic War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Punic_War","aliases":["Second Punic War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04118"],"tapestryIds":["t63-134ac45d8249"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Hannibal's campaign; Cannae and Zama."},{"id":"LE102-467f0346ef9d221b","title":"Battle of Cannae","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Cannae","aliases":["Battle of Cannae"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0537"],"tapestryIds":["t63-7b27e105b1f4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Hannibal defeats Roman armies."},{"id":"LE102-09c3e8d9d7b0c66d","title":"Battle of Zama","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Zama","aliases":["Battle of Zama"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-061e9342ac50"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Scipio defeats Hannibal."},{"id":"LE102-cab4dfc07b6b0595","title":"Four Pompeian painting styles","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompeian_Styles","aliases":["Four Pompeian painting styles"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-e19176bff314"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Successive wall-painting conventions; eruption in 79 CE provides a terminus."},{"id":"LE102-6970dc1a956b15ce","title":"Basilica: civic type before church type","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Basilica","aliases":["Basilica: civic type before church type"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-3485fc8bf402"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The Roman basilica served civic and legal functions. Christian communities adapted the longitudinal hall type; a basilica is not automatically a cathedral.","built":"-200"},{"id":"LE102-d2e7378883eddb51","title":"Roman concrete and opus caementicium","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Roman%20concrete%20and%20opus%20caementicium","aliases":["Roman concrete and opus caementicium"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-749fc7dfdf95"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Concrete combined aggregate with a binding mortar and allowed flexible mass construction. Brick or stone facing can conceal a concrete core.","built":"-200"},{"id":"LE102-e9d13db12323ca00","title":"Battle of Pydna","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pydna","aliases":["Battle of Pydna"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-51752d0321e4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roman victory over Macedon."},{"id":"LE102-33a001c930da1528","title":"Venus de Milo","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus_de_Milo","aliases":["Venus de Milo"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=058d0311d34413fc6c150fdd.webp","credit":"Livioandronico2013","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_views_of_the_Venus_de_Milo.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=058d0311d34413fc6c150fdd.webp","credit":"Livioandronico2013","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_views_of_the_Venus_de_Milo.jpg","licenseUrl":""},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=058d0311d34413fc6c150fdd.webp","credit":"Livioandronico2013","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_views_of_the_Venus_de_Milo.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04528"],"tapestryIds":["t63-6cc6f896ca5c"],"museumIds":["ART93-t63-6cc6f896ca5c"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Hellenistic sculpture; attribution to Alexandros of Antioch is debated.","assetIds":["ART93-t63-6cc6f896ca5c","REV85-IMAGE-4528"]},{"id":"LE102-8a5c9bc42a18de32","title":"Third Punic War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Punic_War","aliases":["Third Punic War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0089"],"tapestryIds":["t63-9f2ba14e61b4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Destruction of Carthage in 146 BCE."},{"id":"LE102-a585cb8c108c9e2d","title":"Roman destruction of Corinth","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Corinth_(146_BC)","aliases":["Roman destruction of Corinth"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-30468b5a04e7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Greek resistance defeated; distinct from Pydna in 168 BCE."},{"id":"LE102-20929d26cb1a2196","title":"Borghese Gladiator","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borghese_Gladiator","aliases":["Borghese Gladiator"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=be346522d36e1c1018d2102c.webp","credit":"\nAgasias of Ephesus","license":"CC BY 2.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borghese_Gladiator%2C_Louvre_Museum%2C_Paris_2_October_2014.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-3b268ecd1fe9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Signed by Agasias of Ephesus; actually depicts a warrior."},{"id":"LE102-7669d91f760caf2b","title":"Julius Caesar","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar","aliases":["Julius Caesar"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01521","GEN43-Q04403","ARCHED-NEW99-0493","ALPHA-B008-Q707","ALPHA-B011-Q988"],"tapestryIds":["t63-1fbc849d4f6f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roman statesman and general."},{"id":"LE102-69ecc8ab0c2ce731","title":"Aqueducts, roads and Roman urban systems","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Aqueducts%2C%20roads%20and%20Roman%20urban%20systems","aliases":["Aqueducts, roads and Roman urban systems"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-4744725f65ba"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Aqueducts use controlled gradients to transport water; arches are only one part of the system. Roads and urban infrastructure supported imperial administration.","built":"-100"},{"id":"LE102-3ae8aac9c6ee567c","title":"Forum, amphitheatre and theatre","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Forum%2C%20amphitheatre%20and%20theatre","aliases":["Forum, amphitheatre and theatre"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-d1b872994a4a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A forum is a civic space; an amphitheatre surrounds an oval arena; a theatre has a semicircular seating arrangement facing a stage. Function helps identify the plan.","built":"-100"},{"id":"LE102-6dad8c79568e62ab","title":"Vitruvius","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitruvius","aliases":["Vitruvius"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-1a07cd76ea27"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roman author and architect; dates approximate."},{"id":"LE102-eea1dd1da5e607a5","title":"Cleopatra VII","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra","aliases":["Cleopatra VII","Death of Cleopatra VII"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-1bf5d8783199","t63-63ba5de6ba54"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Ptolemaic ruler of Egypt."},{"id":"LE102-42c28bd8db1c0ac8","title":"Augustus","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus","aliases":["Augustus","Augustan settlement"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-4e4ae963f6e5","t63-df98221c6f07"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"First Roman emperor."},{"id":"LE102-b3305201d92882e0","title":"Battle of Pharsalus","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pharsalus","aliases":["Battle of Pharsalus"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0509"],"tapestryIds":["t63-cff492b33665"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Caesar defeats Pompey."},{"id":"LE102-0c77b514490fd2c0","title":"Assassination of Julius Caesar","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Julius_Caesar","aliases":["Assassination of Julius Caesar"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01521"],"tapestryIds":["t63-3760f592d8ea"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"15 March."},{"id":"LE102-fc1a2c9383f9ea03","title":"Laocoön and His Sons","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laoco%C3%B6n_and_His_Sons","aliases":["Laocoön and His Sons"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6a831d171170e433cdf0ca32.webp","credit":"Wilfredor","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laoco%C3%B6n_and_his_sons_group.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=6a831d171170e433cdf0ca32.webp","credit":"Wilfredor","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laoco%C3%B6n_and_his_sons_group.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03715"],"tapestryIds":["t63-f4b1978f5d9d"],"museumIds":["ART93-t63-f4b1978f5d9d"],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dating disputed; commonly late Hellenistic or early Imperial. Not a secure single year.","assetIds":["ART93-t63-f4b1978f5d9d"]},{"id":"LE102-5b1b16a365104b0f","title":"Battle of Actium","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Actium","aliases":["Battle of Actium"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04404","ARCHED-NEW101-0509","ALPHA-B008-Q755"],"tapestryIds":["t63-0a522726ebfd"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Octavian defeats Antony and Cleopatra."},{"id":"LE102-e3a7326b6362b987","title":"De architectura","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_architectura","aliases":["De architectura"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B002-Q123","NEWDER-026","PDF34-Q-005-A","PDF35-Q081-A"],"tapestryIds":["t63-ed460efd47ce"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Ten-book architectural treatise; approximate composition period.","creator":"Vitruvius"},{"id":"LE102-1df2d1ec2ab3decd","title":"Pax Romana","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pax_Romana","aliases":["Pax Romana"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04121","PDF35-Q006-A","PDF35-CON-023-A"],"tapestryIds":["t63-6c406059c5fa"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional period from Augustus to Marcus Aurelius."},{"id":"LE102-a8f7ea4502a3f7c5","title":"Birth of Jesus: estimated range","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chronology_of_Jesus","aliases":["Birth of Jesus: estimated range"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-3e061b75dfbc"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"No year zero; historical estimates differ."},{"id":"LE102-3b2b763c