ional martyrdoms of Peter and Paul","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Peter","aliases":["Traditional martyrdoms of Peter and Paul"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-c4f8f3360bc2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dates and details are not securely established."},{"id":"LE102-6932cd8fc4b7e7a6","title":"Eruption of Vesuvius","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eruption_of_Mount_Vesuvius_in_79_AD","aliases":["Eruption of Vesuvius"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01576","ALPHA-B005-Q450"],"tapestryIds":["t63-acd275ccf92a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Pompeii and Herculaneum."},{"id":"LE102-184e34ff34291069","title":"Five Good Emperors","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nerva%E2%80%93Antonine_dynasty","aliases":["Five Good Emperors"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-4f7da074134c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Nerva, Trajan, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius, Marcus Aurelius."},{"id":"LE102-ff2539e5c301760c","title":"Trajan's Column","kind":"sculpture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trajan's_Column","aliases":["Trajan's Column"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=b9ae33c784fe3c7e55ea2ec4.webp","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trajan%27s_Column_HD.jpg","credit":"Livioandronico2013","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","width":472,"height":1100,"file":"Trajan's_Column_HD.jpg"}],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B005-Q433","PDF34-CON-011-A"],"tapestryIds":["t63-f24f479a5551"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Dedicated in 113; spiral relief narrates the Dacian campaigns.","built":"113","lat":41.89583333,"lon":12.48416667,"coordinateSource":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trajan%27s_Column","resolvedTitle102":"Trajan's Column","assetIds":[],"placeId":"LE102-ff2539e5c301760c"},{"id":"LE102-4058ee112c693768","title":"Arch of Septimius Severus","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arch_of_Septimius_Severus","aliases":["Arch of Septimius Severus"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-041442a8a4db"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roman Forum; commemorates Parthian victories.","built":"203","lat":41.892758,"lon":12.484744,"placeId":"LE102-4058ee112c693768","coordinateSource":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arch_of_Septimius_Severus"},{"id":"LE102-6e0da35ecfa79957","title":"Constitutio Antoniniana","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutio_Antoniniana","aliases":["Constitutio Antoniniana"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01107"],"tapestryIds":["t63-f87fdc093fa0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Caracalla extends Roman citizenship to most free inhabitants."},{"id":"LE102-4acc64de343f31ec","title":"Mani and the emergence of Manichaeism","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manichaeism","aliases":["Mani and the emergence of Manichaeism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-b27c003d3c22"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The founder's approximate lifetime frames the emergence of the religion; not the total duration of the tradition."},{"id":"LE102-6f2f0a8c29cd6bee","title":"Sasanian Empire","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sasanian_Empire","aliases":["Sasanian Empire"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-c7641c64ea68"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Persian dynasty succeeding the Arsacids."},{"id":"LE102-0da11f63c8029e56","title":"Diocletian","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diocletian","aliases":["Diocletian","Reign of Diocletian"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-8ce038357e72","t63-a67bb8dafe41"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roman emperor; birth/death dates vary."},{"id":"LE102-2248466217c5ce89","title":"Decian persecution","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decian_persecution","aliases":["Decian persecution"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01517","ARCHED-NEW101-0517"],"tapestryIds":["t63-cba975813d03"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Empire-wide sacrifice requirement under Decius."},{"id":"LE102-94dff2ad158787b0","title":"Constantine I","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_the_Great","aliases":["Constantine I"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-e87f6b2d4db2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roman emperor."},{"id":"LE102-78b282529e9ba710","title":"Tetrarchy established","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetrarchy","aliases":["Tetrarchy established"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-1cbaad9129d1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Diocletian, Maximian, Galerius and Constantius Chlorus."},{"id":"LE102-d8b4ea20ce360862","title":"Early Christian basilica and central plan","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Early%20Christian%20basilica%20and%20central%20plan","aliases":["Early Christian basilica and central plan"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-f1a4bced97b1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Longitudinal basilicas organise movement towards an apse; centrally planned martyria and baptisteries emphasise a central point. Building function matters.","built":"300"},{"id":"LE102-ccdf813bfd9bc819","title":"Apse, nave, aisles and transept","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Apse%2C%20nave%2C%20aisles%20and%20transept","aliases":["Apse, nave, aisles and transept"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-e0a8fdf319c0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The nave is the principal longitudinal space; aisles run alongside it; a transept crosses it; an apse often terminates the sanctuary. Not every church contains all four.","built":"300"},{"id":"LE102-3dcfea05529f88d3","title":"Battle of the Milvian Bridge","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Milvian_Bridge","aliases":["Battle of the Milvian Bridge"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-539d3a256e25"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Constantine defeats Maxentius."},{"id":"LE102-c42621be0b77d26b","title":"Edict of Milan","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edict_of_Milan","aliases":["Edict of Milan"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01606","ARCHED-NEW99-0653","ARCHED-NEW101-0517"],"tapestryIds":["t63-f01d531f4eac"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Constantine and Licinius agree religious toleration."},{"id":"LE102-b78dca577096d2f5","title":"First Council of Nicaea","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Council_of_Nicaea","aliases":["First Council of Nicaea"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01110","GEN43-Q01462","ARCHED-NEW101-0517"],"tapestryIds":["t63-18d134f96eb1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Nicene creed and the Arian controversy."},{"id":"LE102-90074bb0740a3c77","title":"Dedication of Constantinople","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantinople","aliases":["Dedication of Constantinople"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-c1600339b121"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Constantine's imperial capital."},{"id":"LE102-0ec04d412e94a73c","title":"Reign of Julian","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_(emperor)","aliases":["Reign of Julian"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-31126a5ab724"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Attempted revival of traditional cults."},{"id":"LE102-d06b886ac52cc8fa","title":"Edict of Thessalonica","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edict_of_Thessalonica","aliases":["Edict of Thessalonica"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01111","GEN43-Q01480"],"tapestryIds":["t63-a9312604dea7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Theodosius I and colleagues endorse Nicene Christianity."},{"id":"LE102-1d2031adbc010497","title":"First Council of Constantinople","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Council_of_Constantinople","aliases":["First Council of Constantinople"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-376e844ca994"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Separate event from the edict of 380."},{"id":"LE102-10493ffb254a5d74","title":"Permanent division of imperial rule","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire","aliases":["Permanent division of imperial rule"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-2f5800d46c5d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"After the death of Theodosius I."},{"id":"LE102-f139584a7160b9c9","title":"Sack of Rome by Alaric","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sack_of_Rome_(410)","aliases":["Sack of Rome by Alaric"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-0cc2f4cb79e6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Visigoths enter Rome."},{"id":"LE102-d87fc8281519bdef","title":"Visigothic settlement in Aquitaine","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visigothic_Kingdom","aliases":["Visigothic settlement in Aquitaine"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-e2557d5bf8b7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Kingdom initially centred on Toulouse."},{"id":"LE102-ca8a2519bc664252","title":"Traditional start of Anglo-Saxon migration","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Saxon_settlement_of_Britain","aliases":["Traditional start of Anglo-Saxon migration"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-96c8c50dc709"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Migration was a long process; 449 is a traditional date."},{"id":"LE102-59bac6a3730600c3","title":"Anthemius of Tralles","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthemius_of_Tralles","aliases":["Anthemius of Tralles"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0225"],"tapestryIds":["t63-cf54d34b8f1b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Mathematician and architect; dates approximate."},{"id":"LE102-938a42008c2c51f6","title":"Deposition of Romulus Augustulus","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romulus_Augustulus","aliases":["Deposition of Romulus Augustulus"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW99-0361"],"tapestryIds":["t63-e6d285ed9cd9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional end of the Western Roman Empire."},{"id":"LE102-ef54b0a435fae752","title":"Justinian I","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justinian_I","aliases":["Justinian I"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-29a1ac37754c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Byzantine emperor."},{"id":"LE102-e2de8034295295df","title":"Ostrogothic rule in Italy begins","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ostrogothic_Kingdom","aliases":["Ostrogothic rule in Italy begins"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-96ac7852e03b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Theoderic defeats Odoacer."},{"id":"LE102-ea7709580cc423fb","title":"Pendentives and a dome over a square","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Pendentives%20and%20a%20dome%20over%20a%20square","aliases":["Pendentives and a dome over a square"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-7eb96ec33ff7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Curved triangular pendentives mediate between a square bay and a circular dome base. Distinguish them from squinches, which bridge the corners differently.","built":"500"},{"id":"LE102-498c0a89bfa69e40","title":"Byzantine mosaics and gold grounds","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Byzantine%20mosaics%20and%20gold%20grounds","aliases":["Byzantine mosaics and gold grounds"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-623c33a8c37d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Gold tesserae interact with light and can reduce the sense of ordinary space. Frontal, hierarchical images communicate religious authority; technique and function matter."},{"id":"LE102-f9a294ec1d19423e","title":"Justinian's legal compilation","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corpus_Juris_Civilis","aliases":["Justinian's legal compilation"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW99-0043"],"tapestryIds":["t63-8cfe961532fb"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"First Code 529; revised Code 534; Digest and Institutes 533."},{"id":"LE102-05936c2e310c6f9b","title":"Isidore of Miletus","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isidore_of_Miletus","aliases":["Isidore of Miletus"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0225"],"tapestryIds":["t63-59689100729b"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Architect; approximate activity period, not established lifespan."},{"id":"LE102-6b74e2cbfce1e2a3","title":"Lombards enter Italy","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lombard_Kingdom","aliases":["Lombards enter Italy"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0469"],"tapestryIds":["t63-7bbfbea848de"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Alboin's invasion."},{"id":"LE102-bf7d825c840a96b4","title":"Muhammad","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad","aliases":["Muhammad","Death of Muhammad"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-1d6e1db568af","t63-ef15c210fa30"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Founder of Islam; traditional birth date."},{"id":"LE102-3e83c2672887eee4","title":"Reign of Heraclius","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclius","aliases":["Reign of Heraclius"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-639002e27ecc"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Byzantine emperor."},{"id":"LE102-79ab9d3ad993a466","title":"Hijra","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hijrah","aliases":["Hijra"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-b68311675474"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Muhammad's migration to Medina; Islamic calendar epoch."},{"id":"LE102-3a324e4830e2c942","title":"Lateran Council of 649","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lateran_Council_of_649","aliases":["Lateran Council of 649"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0469"],"tapestryIds":["t63-29a42d5a6dc9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Council under Pope Martin I concerning monothelitism."},{"id":"LE102-d6f6e6a931229608","title":"End of the Sasanian Empire","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yazdegerd_III","aliases":["End of the Sasanian Empire"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-01eb91d3808f"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Death of the last Sasanian ruler."},{"id":"LE102-9a553bb13269457f","title":"Umayyad Caliphate","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umayyad_Caliphate","aliases":["Umayyad Caliphate"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW99-0236"],"tapestryIds":["t63-4b819424df70"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Damascus-based caliphate."},{"id":"LE102-1bf4bdaf7c70edba","title":"Third Council of Constantinople","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Council_of_Constantinople","aliases":["Third Council of Constantinople"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-170dcdde03a3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Condemns monothelitism."},{"id":"LE102-268ce04fccfe00d4","title":"Battle of Tertry","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tertry","aliases":["Battle of Tertry"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0491"],"tapestryIds":["t63-62a4e2a21842"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Pepin of Herstal consolidates power."},{"id":"LE102-5a18ffe9e2355de3","title":"Iconoclasm and the religious image","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Iconoclasm%20and%20the%20religious%20image","aliases":["Iconoclasm and the religious image"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-5300efa81a53"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Byzantine disputes concerned the legitimacy of sacred images, not opposition to every form of art. The restoration of icons in 843 is a key marker."},{"id":"LE102-fc2742418c087a5d","title":"End of the siege of Constantinople","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Constantinople_(717%E2%80%93718)","aliases":["End of the siege of Constantinople"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-9ebdc4de2500"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Byzantine defence against the Umayyads."},{"id":"LE102-c71516d1dd0a4cf3","title":"Battle of Tours / Poitiers","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tours","aliases":["Battle of Tours / Poitiers"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0491"],"tapestryIds":["t63-12ec4137ef61"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Charles Martel defeats an Umayyad force."},{"id":"LE102-7e120ea012690d48","title":"Charlemagne","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlemagne","aliases":["Charlemagne","Imperial coronation of Charlemagne"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0480"],"tapestryIds":["t63-36bac29db89b","t63-efab7f2bae61"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Birth year disputed: 742, 747 or 748."},{"id":"LE102-622205cbed0d3d0f","title":"Abbasid Caliphate: early and Baghdad periods","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbasid_Caliphate","aliases":["Abbasid Caliphate: early and Baghdad periods"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-12a7f5c81d07"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Baghdad founded in 762; Mongol sack in 1258."},{"id":"LE102-ea0000eaaabf2c6e","title":"Pepin the Short becomes king","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepin_the_Short","aliases":["Pepin the Short becomes king"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0480","ARCHED-NEW101-0491"],"tapestryIds":["t63-84be9d018aec"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Beginning of Carolingian royal rule."},{"id":"LE102-dfc1273d4f539c2b","title":"Donation of Pepin","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donation_of_Pepin","aliases":["Donation of Pepin"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04128"],"tapestryIds":["t63-1d81b32e454c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Papal territorial claims in Italy."},{"id":"LE102-2db92c27e96bc139","title":"Charlemagne conquers the Lombard kingdom","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Pavia_(773%E2%80%93774)","aliases":["Charlemagne conquers the Lombard kingdom"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0480"],"tapestryIds":["t63-1eee2d95cfd1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Pavia falls to the Franks."},{"id":"LE102-2f16a448edde3ec1","title":"Palatine Chapel, Aachen","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palatine_Chapel,_Aachen","aliases":["Palatine Chapel, Aachen","Palatine Chapel in Aachen"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0165","ARCHED-NEW101-0222","ARCHED-NEW101-0225"],"tapestryIds":["t63-fe5d3d5590a8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Carolingian octagonal chapel; attributed to Odo of Metz.","built":"792","assetIds":[],"lat":50.7747,"lon":6.08444,"city":"Aachen","style":"Carolingian","creator":"Odo of Metz","coordinateSource":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palatine_Chapel%2C_Aachen","placeId":"LE102-2f16a448edde3ec1"},{"id":"LE102-29e51d01c84007e2","title":"Viking Age","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viking_Age","aliases":["Viking Age"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-33f4dcb13d40"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional European range; expansion and settlement varied by region."},{"id":"LE102-602f136c6ed72b32","title":"Carolingian renewal and classical revival","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Carolingian%20renewal%20and%20classical%20revival","aliases":["Carolingian renewal and classical revival"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-63ff2ceb0094"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Court patronage promoted learning, manuscripts and selected ancient models. Revival is a reinterpretation, not an unchanged survival of Roman culture."},{"id":"LE102-715ee77346309dc1","title":"Classic Maya collapse","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classic_Maya_collapse","aliases":["Classic Maya collapse"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-c21c760a6cef"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Regional process, not one event in 900."},{"id":"LE102-3481657f1743c758","title":"Egbert's overlordship","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecgberht,_King_of_Wessex","aliases":["Egbert's overlordship"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-096b47ccfb49"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Not the definitive unification of England; distinguish 927."},{"id":"LE102-e72840bd6a9d76b6","title":"Treaty of Verdun","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Verdun","aliases":["Treaty of Verdun"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-acdb56bff005"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Carolingian empire partitioned into three kingdoms."},{"id":"LE102-01b64353b4581aba","title":"Traditional beginning of Rurik's rule","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rurik","aliases":["Traditional beginning of Rurik's rule"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-7897c01c47e7"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Traditional chronology of the Rus'."},{"id":"LE102-41765afccf6be068","title":"Treaty of Meerssen","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Meerssen","aliases":["Treaty of Meerssen"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01612"],"tapestryIds":["t63-7470938521f2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Division of Lothair II's kingdom between East and West Francia."},{"id":"LE102-39e859660eca03a3","title":"Traditional capture of Kyiv by Oleg","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oleg_of_Novgorod","aliases":["Traditional capture of Kyiv by Oleg"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-0f5c2f1cb48e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional beginning of Kyiv-centred rule."},{"id":"LE102-aaabad6f9dfe8901","title":"Duchy of Normandy established","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Saint-Clair-sur-Epte","aliases":["Duchy of Normandy established"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-2ab5eb7ec7b8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Settlement associated with Rollo."},{"id":"LE102-e9b21454b376ba69","title":"Æthelstan unites England","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86thelstan","aliases":["Æthelstan unites England"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-7bf2caf46165"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Often regarded as the first king of all England."},{"id":"LE102-2ad5d08ad6d4ba3a","title":"Battle of Lechfeld","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Lechfeld","aliases":["Battle of Lechfeld"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-d0e5f09a2805"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Otto I defeats the Magyars."},{"id":"LE102-01dd791c3a171ea8","title":"Imperial coronation of Otto I","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_I,_Holy_Roman_Emperor","aliases":["Imperial coronation of Otto I"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-0592d323cde1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional foundation date of the Holy Roman Empire."},{"id":"LE102-35a7086c22e067f8","title":"Hugh Capet becomes king","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Capet","aliases":["Hugh Capet becomes king"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-d91f0cc6d289"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Beginning of the Capetian dynasty."},{"id":"LE102-62ef0e1a3584a0a4","title":"Christianisation of Kievan Rus'","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianization_of_Kievan_Rus'","aliases":["Christianisation of Kievan Rus'"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01473"],"tapestryIds":["t63-876b991b23e6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Traditionally associated with Vladimir I's baptism."},{"id":"LE102-9a2b533e504e79b7","title":"Pilgrimage churches and circulation","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Pilgrimage%20churches%20and%20circulation","aliases":["Pilgrimage churches and circulation"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-7af46abf2921"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Ambulatories and radiating chapels can accommodate movement around sacred relics while worship continues. Connect spatial planning with liturgical function.","built":"1000"},{"id":"LE102-347d806ef9c55cff","title":"Romanesque: broad European period","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanesque_art","aliases":["Romanesque: broad European period"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-99dce91286ca"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Approximate stylistic period; regional boundaries differ and overlap Gothic developments."},{"id":"LE102-0a43673cb0675f9f","title":"Romanesque: mass, bays and round arches","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Romanesque","aliases":["Romanesque: mass, bays and round arches"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-bbcc08d8d5d4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Thick masonry, round arches and strongly articulated bays are common identifiers. Vaulting systems and regional traditions vary; a single round arch is not conclusive.","built":"1000"},{"id":"LE102-39d34540ca49964d","title":"William the Conqueror","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_the_Conqueror","aliases":["William the Conqueror"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-830e1b05b8cf"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Approximate birth year."},{"id":"LE102-ce6332b31037a2ee","title":"Henry IV","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_IV,_Holy_Roman_Emperor","aliases":["Henry IV"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01474","GEN43-Q04557","ARCHED-NEW101-0097","ALPHA-B007-Q595"],"tapestryIds":["t63-ed8ab5e3be85"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Emperor associated with Canossa."},{"id":"LE102-af0179f15533e75f","title":"East–West Schism","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East%E2%80%93West_Schism","aliases":["East–West Schism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-a08f5b38e809"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional date in a longer estrangement."},{"id":"LE102-88e7b497bfb96163","title":"Battle of Hastings and Norman conquest","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hastings","aliases":["Battle of Hastings and Norman conquest"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0457"],"tapestryIds":["t63-aca148b80ce0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"William defeats Harold II."},{"id":"LE102-00bdd4a0b547c037","title":"Investiture Controversy","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Investiture_Controversy","aliases":["Investiture Controversy"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01116","ARCHED-NEW101-0098"],"tapestryIds":["t63-e2125978cf2c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Papal and imperial authority over appointments."},{"id":"LE102-1f4f164bc1fdb44a","title":"Walk to Canossa","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_to_Canossa","aliases":["Walk to Canossa"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0496"],"tapestryIds":["t63-ee4e7612155e"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Henry IV seeks absolution from Gregory VII."},{"id":"LE102-d8bc1ac82f88fadc","title":"Traditional foundation of Bologna University","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Bologna","aliases":["Traditional foundation of Bologna University"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-5abe97fc5338"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Conventional institutional foundation date."},{"id":"LE102-e709695d78cccbaa","title":"Council of Clermont","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Clermont","aliases":["Council of Clermont"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0457"],"tapestryIds":["t63-0184ac2bf704"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Urban II calls for the First Crusade."},{"id":"LE102-aa6824bd6c3e299c","title":"First Crusade","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Crusade","aliases":["First Crusade"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW99-0962"],"tapestryIds":["t63-9f0886fa460a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Jerusalem captured in 1099."},{"id":"LE102-acb4517cd32be195","title":"Cathedral, abbey and parish church","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Cathedral%2C%20abbey%20and%20parish%20church","aliases":["Cathedral, abbey and parish church"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-8fccc06b3005"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A cathedral contains a bishop's cathedra; an abbey belongs to a monastic institution; a parish church serves a local community. Size and architectural style do not determine these categories.","built":"1100"},{"id":"LE102-a3a2838b74a125fe","title":"Frederick Barbarossa","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_Barbarossa","aliases":["Frederick Barbarossa"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04129","ARCHED-NEW99-0696","ARCHED-NEW99-0863"],"tapestryIds":["t63-0ccea97f7174"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Hohenstaufen emperor."},{"id":"LE102-db9999c7e98bcbb1","title":"Kingdom of Sicily established","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Sicily","aliases":["Kingdom of Sicily established"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0496","ARCHED-NEW101-0527"],"tapestryIds":["t63-0bebbf554f03"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Roger II crowned king."},{"id":"LE102-c017823a62dc3592","title":"Saladin","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saladin","aliases":["Saladin","Saladin becomes vizier in Egypt"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0527"],"tapestryIds":["t63-7e85b8e8e1e9","t63-05ff2cff61bf"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Birth also given as 1138."},{"id":"LE102-d03fa0211ff3d2b7","title":"Flying buttress and lateral thrust","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Flying%20buttress%20and%20lateral%20thrust","aliases":["Flying buttress and lateral thrust"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-10f25f5e896c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A flying buttress transfers outward thrust across an aisle to an external support. Distinguish the visible arch from the whole buttressing system.","built":"1140"},{"id":"LE102-112125296bcd32cc","title":"Gothic: broad European period","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gothic_art","aliases":["Gothic: broad European period"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-4cf4d37f2996"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A regional stylistic framework, not a precise beginning or ending everywhere."},{"id":"LE102-e231d08b5c7867a4","title":"Gothic: pointed arch, rib vault and buttress","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Gothic","aliases":["Gothic: pointed arch, rib vault and buttress"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-a6a931d36dfe"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The coordinated structural system channels loads and allows taller interiors and larger windows. Gothic is not defined solely by a pointed arch.","built":"1140"},{"id":"LE102-3dfe2601d6ac56f1","title":"Second Crusade","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Crusade","aliases":["Second Crusade"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-1569c413b62c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Campaign following the fall of Edessa."},{"id":"LE102-81067f44cf6a56ed","title":"Rose windows, stained glass and cathedral imagery","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Rose%20windows%2C%20stained%20glass%20and%20cathedral%20imagery","aliases":["Rose windows, stained glass and cathedral imagery"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-c0fc3eb496b3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Coloured glass structures light and conveys religious narratives. Tracery subdivides an opening; it is not the coloured glass itself."},{"id":"LE102-d3ec68b3c560d9b1","title":"Richard I","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_I_of_England","aliases":["Richard I"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW99-0431"],"tapestryIds":["t63-30c85381e00a"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"King of England; Third Crusade."},{"id":"LE102-cc7a7340cae6c51e","title":"John of England","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John,_King_of_England","aliases":["John of England"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-063842c4b5d8"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"King associated with Magna Carta."},{"id":"LE102-55fa776c93b5313f","title":"Ayyubid dynasty in Egypt","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayyubid_dynasty","aliases":["Ayyubid dynasty in Egypt"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-39a53b62a58d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Saladin ends Fatimid rule."},{"id":"LE102-8a1b4f9f4c57b035","title":"Third Crusade","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Crusade","aliases":["Third Crusade"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-711be1e4b172"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Richard I, Philip II and Frederick Barbarossa."},{"id":"LE102-3f6d03e5be6b798a","title":"Teutonic Order founded","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teutonic_Order","aliases":["Teutonic Order founded"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0457","ARCHED-NEW101-0527","ARCHED-NEW101-0536"],"